WEBVTT


00:02:11.873 --> 00:02:14.251
Yeah, Walter. Hi, it's George.


00:02:14.334 --> 00:02:17.087
I know it's my third call on a Saturday,


00:02:17.170 --> 00:02:21.175
but I'm having a bit of a problem
with the Lockwise Helping Hand account.


00:02:21.258 --> 00:02:24.478
Now, I know it's your baby,
and I know you'll straighten it out,


00:02:24.553 --> 00:02:28.854
but, well, I'm thinking of heading into
the office today to see if I can sort it out.


00:02:28.932 --> 00:02:32.186
So, no problems. We'll see you on Monday.


00:02:32.269 --> 00:02:36.149
Don't worry about it.
Give my love to Rebecca. Bye-bye.


00:02:38.316 --> 00:02:40.489
- Barbara, stop it.
- No.


00:02:40.569 --> 00:02:42.742
- You need this.
- No, I will not.


00:02:43.071 --> 00:02:44.197
George!


00:02:44.281 --> 00:02:46.124
George, yes. Where is George?


00:02:46.241 --> 00:02:48.243
- I would like to speak to him.
- I don't know.


00:02:48.326 --> 00:02:50.795
I don't even know who you are, young lady.


00:02:51.913 --> 00:02:53.415
- George.
- Thank God.


00:02:53.498 --> 00:02:55.921
George, who is this young lady?


00:02:56.585 --> 00:02:58.303
- Here, honey.
- That's...


00:02:58.420 --> 00:03:00.172
I can't do this.


00:03:00.255 --> 00:03:01.802
That's my wife, Mom.


00:03:01.923 --> 00:03:04.676
No. She's too young.


00:03:04.801 --> 00:03:06.474
How old is she?


00:03:06.595 --> 00:03:08.222
We were married nine years ago, remember?


00:03:08.305 --> 00:03:09.932
She's nine years old?


00:03:10.015 --> 00:03:13.519
Our marriage is nine years old,
our marriage.


00:03:17.480 --> 00:03:19.949
She's the second one.


00:03:20.984 --> 00:03:23.737
No. I adored the other one.


00:03:23.820 --> 00:03:26.619
I know, Mom, but,
you know, she tried to kill me.


00:03:26.698 --> 00:03:29.167
No, she didn't.
That was just a little hit-and-run.


00:03:29.284 --> 00:03:31.958
Yeah, well, I was in traction for two months.


00:03:32.037 --> 00:03:33.960
I don't remember that.


00:03:35.457 --> 00:03:37.835
- Here you go.
- I like this one.


00:03:37.959 --> 00:03:40.803
- Well, that's the most popular one.
- Yeah.


00:03:41.171 --> 00:03:42.673
There you go.


00:03:46.885 --> 00:03:49.684
- We aren't done with this.
- Yes, I know. I know.


00:03:49.804 --> 00:03:52.432
And why are you wearing a shirt and tie
on a Saturday?


00:03:52.515 --> 00:03:54.313
I have to go into the office.


00:03:54.434 --> 00:03:56.482
- You're going into the office?
- Yes.


00:03:56.603 --> 00:03:58.230
- When?
- Now.


00:03:58.313 --> 00:04:01.317
George, aren't you forgetting something?


00:04:02.359 --> 00:04:04.327
No, I'm not.


00:04:05.278 --> 00:04:06.655
I love you.


00:04:06.780 --> 00:04:09.829
Nice try. Your son.


00:04:09.950 --> 00:04:13.454
You promised him you would take him
to his baseball game today.


00:04:13.536 --> 00:04:16.540
I'm not telling him this time. You do it.


00:04:16.665 --> 00:04:21.216
Honey, I'll be back in time.
The game doesn't start until 2:00.


00:04:21.336 --> 00:04:22.337
1100.


00:04:22.963 --> 00:04:24.636
I'll be back.


00:04:24.798 --> 00:04:28.018
Mom, Dad, Grandma isn't eating.


00:04:29.511 --> 00:04:32.685
God, I hate old people.


00:04:32.681 --> 00:04:34.524
Watch your mouth, young lady.


00:04:34.641 --> 00:04:37.485
Why? It's not like she understands
anything we're saying.


00:04:37.560 --> 00:04:40.234
You know what? I've had
just about enough of your attitude.


00:04:41.356 --> 00:04:43.404
Hello? You listening?


00:04:43.692 --> 00:04:47.367
iPod. They were made
to ignore the stepmother.


00:04:47.487 --> 00:04:48.454
George?


00:04:48.530 --> 00:04:51.534
Honey, would you take those things off,
please, and listen to your mother?


00:04:52.492 --> 00:04:54.870
Okay, she is not my mother.


00:04:55.412 --> 00:04:57.210
She's the mother of that thing.


00:04:57.372 --> 00:04:59.090
- You're the thing.
- You're a thing.


00:04:59.207 --> 00:05:01.835
- You're a thing, sister.
- Don't call me that.


00:05:02.419 --> 00:05:05.889
Dad, I'm really excited
about the game today.


00:05:06.006 --> 00:05:08.350
It's gonna be so cool having you there.


00:05:09.050 --> 00:05:13.055
Jeremy's dad is always there,
but he yells at me if I miss the ball.


00:05:13.179 --> 00:05:15.181
Well, that's not gonna happen today, son.


00:05:15.265 --> 00:05:16.892
Now, I've got to run to the office,


00:05:17.017 --> 00:05:19.566
but I'll be back in time
to take you to your game.


00:05:19.644 --> 00:05:20.987
You promise?


00:05:22.063 --> 00:05:23.906
Scout's honor.


00:05:28.987 --> 00:05:29.988
Don't forget. 1:00.


00:05:30.071 --> 00:05:31.163
He's not coming.


00:05:31.990 --> 00:05:34.413
<i>That was the Star Trek sign.</i>


00:05:34.492 --> 00:05:36.085
He's a Trekkie.


00:05:36.578 --> 00:05:38.080
And so am I.


00:06:06.066 --> 00:06:07.943
- Morning, Jackie.
- Hello.


00:06:08.026 --> 00:06:10.449
Don't you wish it was this quiet every day?


00:06:10.528 --> 00:06:12.747
Be careful what you wish for.


00:06:26.127 --> 00:06:29.097
<i>Gotta be mine</i>


00:06:33.218 --> 00:06:35.767
<i>Gotta be strong</i>


00:06:36.137 --> 00:06:38.936
<i>A little While</i>


00:06:39.057 --> 00:06:42.732
<i>And you got nothing to be guilty of</i>


00:06:42.811 --> 00:06:44.734
<i>You might not wanna sing that song.</i>


00:06:53.905 --> 00:06:55.248
Okay. Shred everything.


00:06:55.532 --> 00:06:57.534
My shredder's broken.
I need another shredder!


00:06:57.617 --> 00:06:58.994
- Here we go!
- Who's got one?


00:06:59.077 --> 00:07:00.329
Don't leave any evidence. Nothing. Okay?


00:07:00.411 --> 00:07:02.084
- Put 'em in a box!
- Let me through. Let me through.


00:07:02.163 --> 00:07:05.007
Shred everything! Here, here. Right here!


00:07:08.878 --> 00:07:10.130
All the boxes!


00:07:12.382 --> 00:07:14.635
All right. Grab those two!
What are you doing?


00:07:15.885 --> 00:07:17.637
Just get it in here! Anything!


00:07:20.431 --> 00:07:21.853
I got one more!


00:07:21.933 --> 00:07:23.776
- Is it the last quarter?
- Yeah.


00:07:26.104 --> 00:07:27.196
Dump everything!


00:07:29.274 --> 00:07:30.366
George, come in here, buddy.


00:07:31.818 --> 00:07:33.161
Come in, come in, come in.


00:07:33.278 --> 00:07:35.030
Walter, what's going on?


00:07:35.113 --> 00:07:37.036
Hey, listen, pull your money out of the bank,


00:07:37.115 --> 00:07:39.789
cash in all your stocks and bonds
by 10:00 a.m. Monday morning.


00:07:40.285 --> 00:07:41.332
Why?


00:07:41.744 --> 00:07:44.918
Well, CNN is doing
one of those investigative reports


00:07:44.998 --> 00:07:46.716
about Lockwise Industries.


00:07:48.543 --> 00:07:51.046
That's fantastic.
That'll be great for business.


00:07:51.171 --> 00:07:55.017
Not really. They're gonna say we've been
running a Ponzi scheme for seven years.


00:07:56.676 --> 00:07:59.725
Well, they can't say that, Walter.
That's libelous.


00:07:59.846 --> 00:08:03.567
I mean, this firm's been operating
successfully for over 100 years.


00:08:03.683 --> 00:08:07.358
Yeah, yeah, they're focusing
on the charity division, Helping Hands.


00:08:07.437 --> 00:08:10.486
Helping Hands has been going strong
for over eight years.


00:08:10.565 --> 00:08:11.908
I should know. I'm CFO.


00:08:13.067 --> 00:08:14.239
Yeah. Yeah, you are.


00:08:14.319 --> 00:08:16.617
Could you say that again,
the part about the CFO?


00:08:17.447 --> 00:08:19.745
I'm CFO. I should know.


00:08:20.158 --> 00:08:22.035
Right. Perfect, perfect. Thanks.


00:08:22.160 --> 00:08:26.882
Walter, are they reporting
that it's our division?


00:08:27.248 --> 00:08:28.716
Yeah. Your division.


00:08:29.167 --> 00:08:30.714
But I have all the records.


00:08:31.294 --> 00:08:33.137
Say that again.


00:08:34.047 --> 00:08:36.175
But I have all the records.


00:08:36.341 --> 00:08:38.218
Perfect. Now shred them.


00:08:38.718 --> 00:08:40.095
- Walter.
- Yeah.


00:08:40.845 --> 00:08:42.142
What are you saying?


00:08:42.513 --> 00:08:44.186
I'm saying that all the monies


00:08:44.265 --> 00:08:49.112
that came into Lockwise Industries'
Helping Hands charity investment group


00:08:49.187 --> 00:08:51.406
are part of a big, old Ponzi scheme.


00:08:52.398 --> 00:08:53.524
What?


00:08:54.192 --> 00:08:55.489
Yeah. Christ.


00:08:55.568 --> 00:08:58.037
It worked for a while.


00:08:58.404 --> 00:09:00.998
I almost feel bad for hanging
you out to dry like this.


00:09:01.074 --> 00:09:03.793
You should see your face, dude.


00:09:04.285 --> 00:09:07.664
And by the way,
this is not gonna be pretty for you.


00:09:07.747 --> 00:09:09.749
I feel awful.


00:09:09.832 --> 00:09:11.084
Horrible.


00:09:11.167 --> 00:09:12.714
What? But...


00:09:13.419 --> 00:09:14.466
For me?


00:09:14.545 --> 00:09:16.798
You were a lowly accountant, remember?


00:09:16.881 --> 00:09:20.681
And then I pull you out of bookkeeping
and make you the CFO.


00:09:20.760 --> 00:09:23.889
I mean, you had no experience
whatsoever. None. None at all.


00:09:23.972 --> 00:09:27.693
I had worked here five years
prior to that, Walter.


00:09:27.767 --> 00:09:32.694
- I was working hard. I thought I earned it.
- You did work hard.


00:09:32.814 --> 00:09:36.614
Nobody earns it around here.
I had to bang my way to the top.


00:09:36.693 --> 00:09:39.242
And there's a lot of big women
on the Board of Directors here.


00:09:39.320 --> 00:09:42.369
And that was hard,
and it was hard to stay hard.


00:09:42.448 --> 00:09:45.076
So don't talk to me about "hard."


00:09:45.285 --> 00:09:50.257
Okay? You were paid a seven-figure salary
for exactly this reason.


00:09:50.790 --> 00:09:52.133
What reason?


00:09:53.126 --> 00:09:57.176
So you could take the fall.
Man, you've been paid to be screwed.


00:09:57.255 --> 00:09:59.474
Kind of jealous. Oh, well.


00:09:59.716 --> 00:10:03.471
Walter, I knew nothing about this.


00:10:03.553 --> 00:10:05.931
Yeah, I know. I know. Sorry.


00:10:06.472 --> 00:10:08.725
Would have ruined it if you had, kind of.


00:10:10.643 --> 00:10:14.273
Well, that explains why I couldn't get
those accounts to balance.


00:10:14.355 --> 00:10:15.948
Now you're thinking.


00:10:17.066 --> 00:10:20.195
What about the charities?
Walter, 82 charities.


00:10:20.320 --> 00:10:21.913
They think their monies are safe.


00:10:21.988 --> 00:10:24.116
I'm handing you over to the Feds,


00:10:24.282 --> 00:10:28.037
and all you care about
is the stupid charities?


00:10:29.495 --> 00:10:30.872
By the way, there's only 12 charities.


00:10:32.165 --> 00:10:34.167
There's 82 charities.


00:10:34.625 --> 00:10:38.801
No, there's 12. The other 70 companies
were set up by the Malone family.


00:10:40.173 --> 00:10:41.299
Awkward.


00:10:43.676 --> 00:10:44.973
The Mafia Malones?


00:10:45.219 --> 00:10:47.472
You've been laundering money, dude.


00:10:47.555 --> 00:10:50.308
Yeah, this is gonna be really awful for you.


00:10:51.768 --> 00:10:53.395
Hey, man, be careful
when you start your car.


00:10:56.397 --> 00:10:58.741
This is not happening.


00:10:59.233 --> 00:11:02.737
A Ponzi scheme? A Ponzi scheme?


00:11:03.654 --> 00:11:07.579
Walter, where are the investors' monies?


00:11:09.827 --> 00:11:12.455
Walter? Walter!


00:11:20.004 --> 00:11:25.932
Okay, calm down. Calm, calm, calm.
Calm down.


00:11:26.010 --> 00:11:27.887
That's it. That's it.


00:11:27.970 --> 00:11:30.769
Just calm down.


00:11:31.641 --> 00:11:35.145
I'm not calming. I'm not calming.
I'm not calming.


00:11:50.618 --> 00:11:52.871
<i>- Hey, boss, just the person I wanna see.
- What do you have?</i>


00:11:52.954 --> 00:11:55.548
So I've been looking
into the Malone crime family, right?


00:11:55.623 --> 00:11:56.624
And the more I look at them,


00:11:56.749 --> 00:11:58.376
I'm finding that they're connected
to this company


00:11:58.459 --> 00:12:00.882
that does a lot of charity
investment work, called Lockwise.


00:12:00.962 --> 00:12:01.963
Yes?


00:12:02.046 --> 00:12:03.969
I think they may be
laundering money through them.


00:12:04.090 --> 00:12:06.468
- We've been after these guys for years.
- Yeah.


00:12:06.551 --> 00:12:08.645
Why don't you see
what you can find out, okay?


00:12:08.719 --> 00:12:10.062
Okay.


00:12:10.138 --> 00:12:11.640
Thanks a lot.


00:13:13.534 --> 00:13:14.877
George?


00:13:18.789 --> 00:13:21.463
I've been calling you for hours.


00:13:22.960 --> 00:13:25.213
Yeah, I know. I know.


00:13:25.880 --> 00:13:26.927
How is he?


00:13:27.548 --> 00:13:30.552
- He was upset, but he'll be fine.
- That's good.


00:13:30.801 --> 00:13:32.474
Is it true?


00:13:33.429 --> 00:13:34.476
What?


00:13:34.555 --> 00:13:37.399
Come on, George.
Don't play games with me.


00:13:37.475 --> 00:13:40.149
All the wives were talking about it
at the field today.


00:13:41.896 --> 00:13:43.068
Honey.


00:13:43.481 --> 00:13:47.531
I swear I had no idea this was going on.


00:13:47.610 --> 00:13:48.611
Okay? None.


00:13:48.736 --> 00:13:51.706
I walked into the office,
and there's Walter, and he's saying,


00:13:51.781 --> 00:13:54.580
"Why don't you shred stuff?
Shred whatever you have.


00:13:54.659 --> 00:13:56.878
"Shred what's in your desk.
Just shred everything."


00:13:56.953 --> 00:13:58.580
And I'm going, "What's going on?"


00:13:58.663 --> 00:14:00.586
And he's saying,
"You're gonna take the fall for this,


00:14:00.665 --> 00:14:04.715
"because it's a Ponzi scheme.
It's a Ponzi scheme, and you're the one.


00:14:04.794 --> 00:14:07.217
"You're going down,
'cause you're the CFO."


00:14:07.296 --> 00:14:12.268
You know? I mean, they gave
Bernie Madoff 200 years, honey.


00:14:12.343 --> 00:14:15.438
What do you think they're gonna do to me?
What do you think they're gonna do?


00:14:15.596 --> 00:14:18.395
And what's gonna happen with the kids?
What's gonna happen?


00:14:18.474 --> 00:14:20.943
Howie's afraid, you know,
"Dad, you missed a game."


00:14:21.018 --> 00:14:23.316
<i>I'm gonna miss 38 seasons.</i>


00:14:23.437 --> 00:14:25.815
Sweetheart, I'm in trouble.


00:14:27.191 --> 00:14:30.115
- Calm down.
- Okay.


00:14:32.446 --> 00:14:34.448
- We need to get a lawyer.
- A lawyer.


00:14:34.532 --> 00:14:36.830
And then you need to go to your mom's


00:14:36.951 --> 00:14:38.669
and go find your mom's Valium.


00:14:38.786 --> 00:14:40.709
Get a Valium out of my mom's purse.


00:14:40.788 --> 00:14:43.086
- Okay. Can you do that? Like right now.
- Okay.


00:14:43.165 --> 00:14:44.792
And you need to calm down.


00:14:45.459 --> 00:14:47.086
- Honey.
- It's gonna be okay.


00:14:47.169 --> 00:14:48.671
- It will be. It will be.
- Yes.


00:14:48.796 --> 00:14:51.970
You know, minimum security.
It's not that bad.


00:14:53.175 --> 00:14:54.392
Hey, Madea.


00:14:54.844 --> 00:14:58.144
Hey, Lorraine, how you doing?
Good to see you.


00:15:03.311 --> 00:15:05.484
Lord, it's a zoo up in there
on the first of the month.


00:15:14.488 --> 00:15:16.991
Excuse me, ma'am. You wanna take this?
I don't feel like taking it back.


00:15:17.074 --> 00:15:19.452
Thank you so much.
It's crazy up in there. Be careful.


00:15:19.535 --> 00:15:21.663
They ain't taking that EBT card.
They stopped taking that.


00:15:21.746 --> 00:15:23.748
I got to go somewhere else that take that.


00:15:24.206 --> 00:15:27.335
Yeah, I got to go burn up my EBT card.


00:15:34.175 --> 00:15:36.018
Give me your money.


00:15:38.679 --> 00:15:41.148
Give me your money.


00:15:42.475 --> 00:15:44.728
That's a cute little gun you got, boy.
Get out this car.


00:15:44.810 --> 00:15:50.112
Lady, I will stab and shoot you.
Give me your money.


00:15:50.191 --> 00:15:52.364
Son, I'm gonna tell you this one time, okay?


00:15:52.443 --> 00:15:54.992
I want you to get out of this car
and go on about your business.


00:15:55.071 --> 00:15:56.414
Go get you a job.


00:15:56.530 --> 00:15:59.204
You ain't supposed to be stealing
from nobody working as hard as I...


00:15:59.283 --> 00:16:01.456
What the hell you got to come over here
and steal from the poor for?


00:16:01.535 --> 00:16:04.334
Get out the car. This is your warning, son.
Get out the car. Now, go on.


00:16:04.413 --> 00:16:06.086
Then give me your money!


00:16:06.290 --> 00:16:09.419
I worked for years to get my Social Security.
Now, I finally got it.


00:16:09.543 --> 00:16:10.635
I ain't on no fixed income.


00:16:10.711 --> 00:16:12.429
<i>I'm on a broke income,
'cause I'm broke as hell.</i>


00:16:12.546 --> 00:16:14.014
Now, I want you
to get the hell out of this car.


00:16:14.090 --> 00:16:17.594
This is your chance. Get out of the car, son.
Go on, now. Go get you a job.


00:16:17.718 --> 00:16:20.096
I'm gonna ask you one more time,
old woman.


00:16:20.221 --> 00:16:21.564
I'm gonna tell you one more time.


00:16:21.639 --> 00:16:26.236
Look here! Get out of this car.
Go find you a job. Do you understand me?


00:16:26.310 --> 00:16:28.984
They got people all over the world
that is working hard,


00:16:29.063 --> 00:16:31.486
and y'all young thugs gonna come
try to take money from somebody.


00:16:31.565 --> 00:16:33.317
That makes me mad.
Now, you about to make me mad.


00:16:33.401 --> 00:16:35.403
You about to piss me off.
Now, get on out the car, son.


00:16:35.569 --> 00:16:37.116
- I'm gonna count to three.
- Okay.


00:16:37.238 --> 00:16:41.994
One, two, three.


00:16:43.953 --> 00:16:45.330
Four


00:16:46.622 --> 00:16:47.748
Five.


00:16:48.082 --> 00:16:51.552
I thought you was gonna count to three.
Son. Son, son, let me tell you something.


00:16:51.627 --> 00:16:53.504
Get out the car
and go on about your business.


00:16:53.587 --> 00:16:56.966
Now, this is your last chance.
This is your last chance. Now I got to go.


00:16:57.091 --> 00:17:01.597
One more time. One, two...


00:17:01.679 --> 00:17:02.931
Three!


00:17:09.103 --> 00:17:10.320
Let's go this way.


00:17:10.855 --> 00:17:13.028
Put your seat belt on.
You need a car seat?


00:17:13.607 --> 00:17:14.984
Come get my money!


00:17:15.317 --> 00:17:17.820
Trying to take my damn money
that I worked this hard for.


00:17:19.613 --> 00:17:20.785
Lady!


00:17:20.948 --> 00:17:22.495
I don't got insurance, lady!


00:17:23.701 --> 00:17:24.998
Slow down! Slow down!


00:17:25.161 --> 00:17:27.710
You're screaming
straight up like a little biatch!


00:17:27.872 --> 00:17:28.964
I want to go home!


00:17:32.293 --> 00:17:35.513
You want the money? You come get it.
I come get the money.


00:17:35.629 --> 00:17:37.506
- I'm a real thug! I'm a real thug!
- You crazy!


00:17:37.631 --> 00:17:39.053
Oh, my God!


